// A `{name}` HOLE NAMING NOTHING — REFUSED, at the hole's own position.
//
// `{name}` is resolved at expansion time in the frame being lowered, so
// a name with no binding there is a compile error and not a `?` in the
// output. It must say WHICH name, and it must point at the HOLE: a
// diagnostic on the format string would put the reader at the opening
// quote of a forty-byte format and leave them counting bytes.
//
// "wrong argument count" is the answer this must NOT give. The call
// passes the argument its ONE positional hole wants, and it is correct;
// `total` is the mistake, and a count is silent about which of the two
// is wrong.
//
// A string literal cannot span source lines — a raw newline inside one
// is `LexFault.UnterminatedString` — so the byte offset of the `{` in
// the literal's raw text IS a column offset, exactly. Both compilers
// compute the column that way, `gen_c_print.report_in_format` and
// `bootstrap/gen_c.py`'s `fmt_span`, and this file is what holds them to
// the same answer.
//
// position: the `{` of `{total}`, not the literal and not the call.

main = (env: Env) Res<i32, IoError> {
    subtotal = 7;
    println("{subtotal} of {total}, plus {}", 2);
    Ok(0);
}
